{"key":"enterprise/T1137.005","id":"T1137.005","name":"Outlook Rules","domain":"enterprise","level":"subtechnique","parent_id":"T1137","tactics":["persistence"],"platforms":["Windows","Office Suite"],"environments":["cloud-hosted-endpoint","onprem"],"environment_basis":"project_taxonomy_from_upstream_platforms","summary":"Adversaries may abuse Microsoft Outlook rules to obtain persistence on a compromised system. Outlook rules allow a user to define automated behavior to manage email messages. A benign rule might, for example, automatically move an email to a particular folder in Outlook if it contains specific words from a specific sender. Malicious Outlook rules can be created that can trigger code execution when an adversary sends a specifically crafted email…","source_url":"https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1137/005","source_stix_id":"attack-pattern--3d1b9d7e-3921-4d25-845a-7d9f15c0da44","source_modified":"2025-10-24T17:48:41.026Z","source_object_version":"1.2","telemetry":{"status":"mapped","components":[{"id":"DC0038","name":"Application Log Content","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/datacomponents/DC0038","stix_id":"x-mitre-data-component--9c2fa0ae-7abc-485a-97f6-699e3b6cf9fa","page":"telemetry/DC0038/"},{"id":"DC0064","name":"Command Execution","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/datacomponents/DC0064","stix_id":"x-mitre-data-component--685f917a-e95e-4ba0-ade1-c7d354dae6e0","page":"telemetry/DC0064/"},{"id":"DC0016","name":"Module Load","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/datacomponents/DC0016","stix_id":"x-mitre-data-component--c0a4a086-cc20-4e1e-b7cb-29d99dfa3fb1","page":"telemetry/DC0016/"},{"id":"DC0032","name":"Process Creation","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/datacomponents/DC0032","stix_id":"x-mitre-data-component--3d20385b-24ef-40e1-9f56-f39750379077","page":"telemetry/DC0032/"}],"strategies":[{"id":"DET0095","name":"Detect Persistence via Malicious Outlook Rules","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/detectionstrategies/DET0095","stix_id":"x-mitre-detection-stra